 ### [Gaussian Splashing](1387-gaussian-splashing.md)
-Gaussian Splashing (GSP) combines 3D Gaussian Splatting with Position-Based Dynamics (PBD) to simulate fluids, deformable bodies, and rigid objects. It solves the limitation of vanilla 3DGS, which lacks well-defined appearance properties for translucent/specular fluids, by enriching Gaussian kernels with material parameters (diffusiveness, specularity, roughness) and aligning kernel orientation with surface normals. Choose this when interactive, physically-based rendering of deformable objects from novel views is required.
+Gaussian Splashing combines 3D Gaussian Splatting with Position-Based Dynamics to simulate fluids, deformable bodies, and rigid objects. It distinguishes itself from vanilla 3DGS by enriching Gaussian kernels with material parameters and aligning kernel orientation with surface normals to eliminate spiky noise. Choose this when interactive, physically-based rendering of deformable objects from novel views is required [G].
 
 ### [Position Based Fluids](1765-position-based-fluids.md)
-Position Based Fluids (PBF) is a Lagrangian particle-based method that enforces incompressibility by iteratively correcting particle positions based on density constraints. It distinguishes itself from Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) by treating fluid dynamics as a constraint satisfaction problem rather than solving Navier-Stokes equations via pressure gradients, offering superior stability for incompressible flows. Choose this for real-time, stable fluid simulation where meshing is undesirable.
